				"date": "2026-10-02"
			}
		],
		"notes": "The vendor and product id pairs Walkplay's product catalog lists under SchemeNo11 (data/catalogs/walkplay.json; this match is generated from it, D51), followed by what only devicePEQ 0617f38 lists: the scheme's product ids under the five vendor ids the catalog never names (most of those pairs don't exist), and product ids the catalog never names (0x129d, 0xc20c, 0xc20e) under devicePEQ's other vendor ids. A device with its own profile matches that instead of this group. Reported quirk, not corrected (D39): devicePEQ measured an EPZ TP13 placing bands about 2.25% below the frequency sent, with Q coming out lower toward high frequencies, and applies both to every SchemeNo11 device. Vendor apps send and show frequencies as they are, and so does this profile. Walkplay's app gives this scheme 8 bands of PK, LS, HP and LP, with no high shelf (Walkplay's web app hides it too); devicePEQ gives it the same 8 bands and types."
	}
